      "writtenOn": "2018-12-06T21:41:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1) this comment only explains why I\u0027ve done it. it\u0027s not public, and it\u0027s subject to change without notice. That\u0027s why I put a comment and not a docstring. But the short version is that the only time we currently would have 2 is for LTE+CDMA. Otherwise, it\u0027s always one. Once we add 5G NSA we will have LTE + 5G, so there will be 2.\n\n2) This makes adding elements more efficient, but it\u0027s also not a hard restriction, just a very minor performance optimization. But... if the lower layer reports 3, which could be something like CDMA + LTE + 5G that\u0027s not an error, just unusual.",
